# RELASI + KONEKSI Project Core Rules

This project follows the **PRD v2.0 (`PRD_RELASI_KONEKSI_Ver 2.docx`)** as the single source of truth. Do not invent features, pages, fields, or libraries not specified in the PRD.

## Binding Constraints

- **STRICT RULE violations** are implementation failures
- If requirements are ambiguous or missing, **stop and ask** the human team
- Anything labeled "Out of scope" must NOT be built, scaffolded, or stubbed

## Approved Tech Stack (Exhaustive - No Additions Without Approval)

| Layer | Technology | Constraints |
|-------|------------|-------------|
| Framework | Next.js App Router | TypeScript required. **NO Pages Router** |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS | **NO other CSS frameworks, NO styled-components, NO CSS-in-JS** |
| CMS | Sanity (branded "KONEKSI") | Free tier. Sanity Studio for villagers |
| i18n | next-intl | Subpath routing `/id` and `/en` only |
| Rich text | @portabletext/react | Official Portable Text renderer |
| Video | YouTube embeds only | Lazy-loaded facade (`LazyYouTubeEmbed`) |
| Flip-book | react-pageflip | For the Media booklets |
| Animation | framer-motion | Entrance/reveal only; keep bundles small |
| Social feed | Instagram Graph API | Server-side + ISR; env token; graceful fallback |
| Hosting | Vercel (free/hobby tier) | Auto-deploy from main branch |

## Rendering Strategy

- **SSG with ISR** for article pages (revalidate 60s or webhook)
- **Static** for all other pages
- **NO client-side data fetching** for primary page content

## Folder Structure

```
app/[locale]/          # Routes with locale param
components/            # Reusable components
lib/sanity/            # Sanity client, queries, URL builders
data/                  # Hardcoded content (TypeScript files)
messages/              # Translation JSON (id.json, en.json)
public/                # Static assets
```

## Content Model (PRD v2.0)

- **Sanity (KONEKSI):** 4 article types (`artikel_berita/sejarah/partnership/liputan`), `wisata`, `desa`, `galeri` + `galeri_video` (party adat/kkn), plus `category`.
- **Hardcoded data files:** booklet, maps, downloads (after-movie + guidebook), home videos.
- **Instagram Graph API:** the Beranda feed (server-side, ISR, graceful fallback).
- See the `allowed-routes`, `data-architecture`, and `sanity-schemas` rules for specifics.

## Non-Goals (Out of Scope for MVP)

- No homestay / booking / payment / reservation system
- No user accounts, login, comments, or membership
- No villager CMS access beyond the 6 approved document types
- No self-hosted video (YouTube embeds only)
- No native mobile app
